    <node id="pattern:roundabout_sideswipe_hgv">
      <data key="d0">collision_pattern</data>
      <data key="d6">roundabout_sideswipe_hgv</data>
      <data key="d7">HGV Sideswipe on Roundabout</data>
      <data key="d8">A large vehicle (truck/HGV) enters a roundabout and its swept turning path encroaches on an adjacent smaller vehicle, causing a side scrape.</data>
      <data key="d9">["Large vehicle and smaller vehicle entering roundabout side-by-side", "Smaller vehicle suddenly stops on roundabout after truck passes", "Truck continues without stopping (scrape-and-leave)", "No rear-end impact visible - damage is lateral", "Gap between vehicles narrows as they navigate the curve"]</data>
      <data key="d10">HGV enters outer lane -&gt; turning arc exceeds lane width -&gt; trailer encroaches inner lane -&gt; contact -&gt; car stops, HGV continues</data>
      <data key="d11">["WRONG: Vehicle described as inexplicably stopped (the stop was CAUSED by the sideswipe)", "WRONG: Later-arriving vehicle blamed for collision (they merely navigated around)", "WRONG: Impact classified as rear-end when actually lateral", "WRONG: Truck not identified as involved because it left the scene"]</data>
      <data key="d12">["truck", "car"]</data>
      <data key="d13">["roundabout"]</data>
      <data key="d14">["sideswipe", "swept path", "roundabout", "truck", "HGV", "scrape"]</data>
      <data key="d15">A green Yodel truck and black SUV approach a multi-lane roundabout. Truck in outer lane, SUV in inner lane. Both enter at ~15s. Between 17-19s the truck rear swings into SUV lane. SUV stops at ~20s after being scraped. Truck continues. Later vehicles (van ~25s, red SUV ~38s) just navigate around the stopped SUV.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="pattern:rear_end_stationary">
      <data key="d0">collision_pattern</data>
      <data key="d6">rear_end_stationary</data>
      <data key="d7">Rear-End Collision with Stationary Vehicle</data>
      <data key="d8">A moving vehicle collides with the rear of a stationary vehicle. Classic failure-to-observe.</data>
      <data key="d9">["Clear closing speed between moving and stationary vehicle", "Impact as sudden deceleration at point of contact", "Both vehicles in same lane before impact", "Post-impact: both stationary, striking vehicle directly behind"]</data>
      <data key="d10">Lead vehicle stationary -&gt; following vehicle fails to observe -&gt; closing speed -&gt; rear-end impact</data>
      <data key="d11">["WRONG: Vehicle passing a stopped car confused with rear-end impact", "WRONG: Vehicle slowing near stopped car assumed to have hit it"]</data>
      <data key="d12">["car", "truck", "van"]</data>
      <data key="d13">["roundabout", "motorway", "urban_road"]</data>
      <data key="d14">["rear-end", "stationary", "following distance", "braking"]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="pattern:hit_and_run_scrape">
      <data key="d0">collision_pattern</data>
      <data key="d6">hit_and_run_scrape</data>
      <data key="d7">Hit-and-Run / Scrape-and-Leave</data>
      <data key="d8">A vehicle makes contact and continues driving without stopping. Common with large vehicles.</data>
      <data key="d9">["One vehicle stops after contact; the other continues", "Departing vehicle shows no behaviour change", "Victim vehicle stops in unusual position mid-lane"]</data>
      <data key="d10">Contact -&gt; victim stops -&gt; striking vehicle continues -&gt; scene appears as if victim stopped for no reason</data>
      <data key="d11">["WRONG: Victim described as inexplicably stopped because striking vehicle left frame", "WRONG: Later-arriving vehicle blamed because actual culprit is gone"]</data>
      <data key="d12">["truck", "car", "van", "bus"]</data>
      <data key="d13">["roundabout", "motorway", "urban_road", "intersection"]</data>
      <data key="d14">["hit and run", "scrape and leave", "departed scene"]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="pattern:roundabout_failure_yield">
      <data key="d0">collision_pattern</data>
      <data key="d6">roundabout_failure_yield</data>
      <data key="d7">Failure to Yield at Roundabout Entry</data>
      <data key="d8">Vehicle enters roundabout without giving way to circulating traffic.</data>
      <data key="d9">["Vehicle enters without slowing while another circulates", "Near-miss or impact at entry point", "Circulating vehicle brakes hard or swerves"]</data>
      <data key="d10">Vehicle A circulating -&gt; Vehicle B enters without yielding -&gt; paths converge -&gt; impact or avoidance</data>
      <data key="d11">["WRONG: Normal give-way waiting confused with near-miss"]</data>
      <data key="d12">["car", "van", "truck"]</data>
      <data key="d13">["roundabout"]</data>
      <data key="d14">["give way", "yield", "roundabout entry", "side impact"]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="pattern:lane_change_sideswipe">
      <data key="d0">collision_pattern</data>
      <data key="d6">lane_change_sideswipe</data>
      <data key="d7">Lane Change Sideswipe</data>
      <data key="d8">Vehicle changes lane without checking blind spot, contacting adjacent vehicle.</data>
      <data key="d9">["Vehicle drifts laterally into occupied lane", "Side-to-side contact, same direction of travel", "No significant speed differential"]</data>
      <data key="d10">Vehicle A in lane 1 -&gt; lane change into lane 2 -&gt; Vehicle B in lane 2 -&gt; lateral contact</data>
      <data key="d11">["WRONG: Misclassified as head-on when both moving same direction"]</data>
      <data key="d12">["car", "van", "truck"]</data>
      <data key="d13">["motorway", "urban_road"]</data>
      <data key="d14">["lane change", "blind spot", "sideswipe", "merge"]</data>
    </node>
    <node id="reg:uk_roundabout_priority">
      <data key="d0">regulation</data>
      <data key="d16">uk_roundabout_priority</data>
      <data key="d17">UK</data>
      <data key="d18">roundabout</data>
      <data key="d19">Give way to traffic from the right when entering a roundabout (Highway Code Rule 185).</data>
      <data key="d20">Vehicles on the roundabout have priority. Entering vehicles must yield.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="reg:uk_lane_discipline">
      <data key="d0">regulation</data>
      <data key="d16">uk_lane_discipline</data>
      <data key="d17">UK</data>
      <data key="d18">roundabout</data>
      <data key="d19">Use left lane for left/straight; right lane for right/full circle (Highway Code Rule 186).</data>
      <data key="d20">Lane position at entry indicates intended exit.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="reg:uk_hgv_swept_path">
      <data key="d0">regulation</data>
      <data key="d16">uk_hgv_swept_path</data>
      <data key="d17">UK</data>
      <data key="d18">general</data>
      <data key="d19">Large vehicles may need more than one lane when turning (Highway Code Rule 221).</data>
      <data key="d20">HGVs encroaching into adjacent lanes is a known sideswipe risk.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="reg:uk_hit_and_run">
      <data key="d0">regulation</data>
      <data key="d16">uk_hit_and_run</data>
      <data key="d17">UK</data>
      <data key="d18">general</data>
      <data key="d19">Failing to stop and report an accident is an offence under Road Traffic Act 1988 s.170.</data>
      <data key="d20">If a vehicle departs after contact, flag as potential offence.</data>
    </node>
